
.container
  .hero-unit{style: 'padding-top: 5px; padding-bottom: 5px'}
    -#%h1 PLAAC
    %p
      %strong PLAAC 
      (Prion-Like Amino Acid Composition) searches protein sequences to identify probable prion subsequences using a
      hidden-Markov model (HMM) algorithm.
      %a{href: '#details'} more details
      -#.muted (Note that the foreground probabilities for the HMM have been updated based on the hits from [1])

.container
%form{action: "#{$config[:apppath]}/find", method:'post', enctype:'multipart/form-data'}
  .container
    .row
      .span12
        - unless @success.nil?
          .alert.alert-success= @success
        - unless @error.nil?
          .alert.alert-error= @error

    .row
      .span12
        %h4 Paste or Upload Protein Sequence*
    .row
      .span10.offset1
        %textarea{id: 'sequence', name:'sequence', size:20, style:'width: 95%;font-family:"Courier New", Courier, monospace'}
        .pull-right
          .help-block.mute.footnote
            *Note that all sequences must contain only valid amino acid identifiers.  Uploaded files
            need to be in
            %a{target:'_blank',href:"http://zhanglab.ccmb.med.umich.edu/FASTA/"}
              FASTA format.
        %input{name:'file', type:'file'}

    .row
      .span12
        %h4 Options
        %hr{style:'margin-top: 0'}

    .row
      .span10.offset1
        %label
          %b Core&nbsp;Length
          .pull-right
            %input.input-mini{id:'len', type:'text', name:'len', value:60, size: 6, style:'display: inline-block'}
        %hr.clear

    .row
      .span10.offset1
        %label
          %b
            Background probabilities
          .pull-right
            %select#organisms.input-medium{ name: 'bg' }
              - @bg_freqs.each do |id, name|
                %option{ value: id, title: name }
                  %em= name
        %hr.clear
    .row
      .span10.offset1
        .background-section.hide
          .pull-right
            %input.input-mini{id:'alpha',name:'alpha', type:'text', value:'100', style:'display: inline-block'}
          %label
            %b
              Relative weighting of background probabilities (
              %em alpha
              )
            .help-block.mute.footnote
              0 meaning all from the FASTA Sequence. 100 meaning all from the selected organism's background frequencies.

            %table{width: '100%'}
              %tr
                %td{colspan:2}
                  %div{id:'alphaSlider'}
              %tr
                %td#file_background{width: '50%'}
                  Proteome-wide background frequencies 
                  %br
                  from FASTA Sequence*
                %td#organism_background{style: 'text-align:right; border-left: 1px solid #ccc;'}
                  Proteome-wide background frequencies 
                  %br
                  from selected organism

          .help-block.mute.footnote *Only appropriate when running across an entire proteome.

    .row
      .span8
      .span4.text-right
        %input#run_analysis.btn.btn-large.btn-primary{type:'submit', value:'Run Analysis'}
    .row
      .span12
        %hr{style: 'border-top: 5px solid #eee'}
    .row
      .span8
        %a{name: 'details'}

        %h4{style:'margin-top:0; padding-top:0'} Algorithm Details
        %p 
          The details of the PLAAC algorithm are described in Albert et al. (2009).  If you use this
          this website, or the underlying code, in any publication, please also cite Lancaster et al. (2013),
          which also describes additional extensions and implementation details of the algorithm.  Code for
          the algorithm, as well as for powering this website is available at
          %a{href:"http://github.com/whitehead/plaac"}
            GitHub
          under the open-source MIT license.
        %blockquote
          Alberti, S., Halfmann, R., King, O., Kapila, A. &amp; Lindquist, S. (2009)
          %br
          %a{target:'_blank',href:"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0092867409002669"}
            A systematic survey identifies prions and illuminates sequence features of prionogenic proteins.
          %em Cell
          137, 146–58.
        %blockquote
          Lancaster, A.K., Nutter-Upham, A., Lindquist, S. &amp; King, O.D. (2013)
          %br
          PLAAC: a web and command-line application to identify proteins with Prion-Like Amino Acid Composition
          %em in preparation
          %br

      .span4
        %h4{style:'margin-top:0; padding-top:0'} Precomputed Proteomes
        %ul.unstyled
          %li
            %a{href:"#{$config[:apppath]}/Scer-all-proteins-2012-07-20.xls"}
              %i.icon-download
              Yeast
              %em (S. cerevisiae)
              (XLS file)
            .muted (most recent: 2012-07-20)


%br.clear


-#Local Variables:
-#indent-tabs-mode: nil
-#End:
